virglrenderer: Venus guest threads stay inside one budget

What: one process-wide count of the threads guest calls make (a render worker and a
fence thread per Venus context, a thread per ring and the ring monitor, a sync thread
per device queue), taken before each is made and given back when it is joined. Past
1024 (OMACVM_VENUS_THREADS for tests) the call fails cleanly: the context is not
made, vkCreateRingMESA ends its context, vkCreateDevice returns
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY, and a log line says so (the 1st, 2nd, 4th ... time).
Venus contexts are also bounded by the open-file limit, read at run time: at most a
sixteenth of the soft limit (a context takes up to 8 files), and the render server's
256 workers.
Why: nothing bounded them. macOS allows 4096 threads per process, and QEMU ends the
process when it cannot make a thread of its own, so a program in the VM that made
contexts, rings (the guest's driver makes a ring per thread that compiles pipelines)
or devices without end could end the VM. QEMU raises its soft open-file limit to
OPEN_MAX (10240) on macOS, so contexts stop at the 256 workers there.
Upstream: OmacVM policy.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-threads.c (contexts, rings, queues, context-files).

